- Exact `GET https://mail.proton.me/api/mail/v4/messages` response projection is
  now content-minimizing: it retains only message `ID`, numeric `Time`, and
  provider `Order`, bounds bodies to 256 KiB and pages to 100 rows, rejects the
  same endpoint's draft-creation `POST`, neighboring endpoints, malformed rows,
  and duplicate IDs, and redacts projected metadata from `Debug` output.
- A CDP Network event state machine now scopes itself to one flattened target
  session and retains only request IDs for exact message-list GET requests. It
  bounds unfinished matching requests to 128 entries, requires an exact
  response URL plus HTTP 200 JSON, and accepts only loading-finished order.
  Redirects away, loading failures, and malformed or repeated lifecycle events
  fail closed. Other sessions, mutation traffic, URLs, query terms, request
  headers, cookies, and tokens are not retained.
- The managed driver now wires that state machine into one explicit diagnostic
  observation. It first proves Mail message mode, enables Network with
  `maxPostDataSize=0`, a 256 KiB per-resource buffer, and a 1 MiB total buffer,
  then reloads the same target. Unsolicited CDP events are classified inline and
  discarded rather than queued; the existing 1 MiB frame cap remains in force.
- After an exact list GET reaches HTTP 200 JSON plus `loadingFinished`, the
  driver calls `Network.getResponseBody` only for that request ID. Decoded JSON
  is immediately reduced to message `ID`, numeric `Time`, provider `Order`, and
  `Total`; base64, malformed, oversized, redirected, failed, or ambiguous
  observations fail closed. Network tracking is disabled on both success and
  projection failure before message mode and origin are revalidated.
- Synthetic driver fixtures inject unrelated URLs plus fake Authorization,
  Cookie, and Set-Cookie fields around the matching request. The returned model
  and debug output contain none of them. The fixture proves `Network.disable`
